## 🔑 Important Implementation Notes

### 1. User ID Handling

**Key Point:** FCM token registration works even when user is **not logged in**!

```javascript
// Option 1: Get from localStorage (if previously logged in)
const userId = localStorage.getItem('userId');

// Option 2: Get from JWT token (if logged in)
const token = localStorage.getItem('token');
const decoded = jwtDecode(token);
const userId = decoded.id;

// Option 3: User input (for first-time users)
const userId = prompt('Enter your user ID:');

// Option 4: From backend auth endpoint
const response = await fetch('/api/auth/me');
const user = await response.json();
const userId = user.id;
```

### 2. Token Refresh Handling

FCM tokens can refresh. Always re-register when token changes:

```javascript
// React Native
messaging().onTokenRefresh((newToken) => {
  registerFCMToken(newToken);
});

// Web
// Token refresh is handled automatically by Firebase SDK
```

### 3. Multiple Devices

Users can have multiple devices. Backend supports this - each device gets its own token.

### 4. Deactivate Token on Logout

```javascript
async function logout() {
  const fcmToken = await getFCMToken(); // Get current token
  
  // Deactivate token
  await fetch('http://localhost:8000/fcm/deactivate', {
    method: 'PUT',
    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
    body: JSON.stringify({ token: fcmToken })
  });
  
  // Continue with logout...
}
```

